5.2.3 Solar Energy Gain
The solar energy transmitted through the glass from the outside environment is the part of solar radiation which is transmitted directly through the glass and the part which is re-emitted from the glass after being absorbed.  In warm and hot climates, this heat energy which is transmitted through the glass has to be limited in-order to achieve PART C STRUCTURAL DESIGN — SECTION 8 GLASS AND GLAZING
thermal comfort for the occupants and also to reduce the energy demands of the building.  Factors that can influence the amount of solar gain through the glazing include:
a) orientation;
b) glazed area;
c) shading devices, both internal and external; and d) properties of the glazing.

