6.1.2 Design Considerations
The following design considerations shall be taken into account in determination of appropriate thickness of glass:
a) Maximum area of glass panel is restricted to 15 m2;
b) Maximum span of glass panel is restricted to 4 m;
c) Aspect ratio of the glass panel should be greater than 1.5.  If it is less than 1.5, next higher available thickness should be selected in order to reduce the stress level;
d) Factor of safety applied is 2.5 considering the variability in strength of glass;
e) Applicable to normal, reflective, laminated, tempered and insulating glass;
f) Applicable to rectangular panels properly secured;
g) Design minimum thickness of laminated glass will be the maximum value of thickness in accordance with Table 2 of accepted standard [C-8(6)]; and h) The parameters listed in (a) to (g) are valid for calculating glass thickness using the empirical relationship in 6.1.3.  For glass sizes larger than those mentioned, any recognized method of analysis may be used for design, in consultation with the manufacturer and the expert in the field.

